{"id": "EUVD-2026-76360", "enisaUuid": "7b7fae3f-8251-3f49-a3da-faf9f9ec3d38", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: plda: Fix IRQ domain leaks in the error paths of plda_init_interrupts()\n\nplda_init_interrupts() initializes IRQ domains and creates IRQ mapping but\ndoes not unwind them when later step fails.\n\nIf platform_get_irq() or either irq_create_mapping() fails\nin plda_init_interrupts(), the domains are never deinitialized. If\nirq_create_mapping() fails, port->intx_irq stays initialized.\n\nHence, remove the IRQ domains in the error path by calling\nplda_pcie_irq_domain_deinit().\n\nSince plda_pcie_irq_domain_deinit() now disposes of the intx_irq and\nmsi_irq mappings itself before removing their domains, the msi_irq\nmapping failure path can go directly to err_irq_domain_deinit instead of\ndisposing of port->intx_irq separately first.\n\nThis issue was found by automated review of sashiko-bot\n\n[mani: commit log]", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:47:03", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01b05cebe1e862e31e382359848d7dca02525a4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4b575052ea65423693726a21826d783cf3f1745e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e54e8d2a0f9c8bf251ae4385ea4f4a68840fedad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/19a30bbb6477bfd7e3109b7a2943e6597ee9de37"], "aliases": ["GHSA-ww3r-fjgm-2rcq", "CVE-2026-89454"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05456fd0-dea8-3594-8f67-b5348e0ec27e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "3ba6e105-ec88-3200-b0d8-073d722bba63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "6e8f3f18-4bf2-3468-b68f-a7cf5595ea9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4602c370bdf6946b4e954a3db0ef5958aac2b7b4 <e54e8d2a0f9c8bf251ae4385ea4f4a68840fedad"}, {"id": "6f30af0f-7cc5-3cab-a63e-c471d4276b38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4602c370bdf6946b4e954a3db0ef5958aac2b7b4 <19a30bbb6477bfd7e3109b7a2943e6597ee9de37"}, {"id": "8346276e-6ffd-3ae4-8d87-ba512b5b8d71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "9a9a1252-b63a-38ef-b029-71272538f312", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "9fb017c1-8b32-3535-83f6-e90c6a037e2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4602c370bdf6946b4e954a3db0ef5958aac2b7b4 <4b575052ea65423693726a21826d783cf3f1745e"}, {"id": "bf5197b5-9eb9-39e4-89d7-7d0696384330", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4602c370bdf6946b4e954a3db0ef5958aac2b7b4 <01b05cebe1e862e31e382359848d7dca02525a4f"}, {"id": "d4a121f2-e5c5-3d88-a90c-8a44f3a2b088", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dcd45b8d-6ea0-3c23-a775-c500444949d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "089ba410-e812-3fbc-9f16-7dd0a6c19631", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}